, a potent climate-warming gas, in the San Francisco Bay Area may be roughly twice as high as official estimates, with most of it coming from biological sources, such as landfills, but natural gas leakage also being an important source, according to a new study, </div> </div> </div><br /> ** I gotta figure out a way to fit this into my SF Ratkin game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12902,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","user":"WISDOMINCHAINS","date":". 02-02-2017, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T17:27:54-08:00","id":1042695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041803-real-life-werewolf-the-apocalypse-inspiration?p=1042612#post1042612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">San Francisco Bay Area methane emissions may be double what we thought</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the headline now. &quot;Bay Area farts prove surprising solution to energy crisis.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T00:10:30-08:00","id":1042850,"title":"","content":"There's a lot good inspirations posted above!. I was a teenager when I've met WoD universe and of course WtA (my beloved game). So, here's my example list:<br /> Music:<br /> Metallica - Where the wild things are. Disposable heroes.<br /> Sepultura - Roots album<br /> Music inspired by cthulutech,(don't remember band name, this morn omina or something similar - pisceris , toltec and other tracks remindes of strane umbal places or trance like garou rites).<br /> Movies: the best were mentioned above. But of course Vikings series and Beowulf remindes me of Get, Brotherhood of the Wolves and similar stuff, Pathfinder<br /> Games: Dead space trilogy - one word - desperation, second: survival at all cost, Upcoming WtA game!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, <br /> <br /> But somewhere here on forum I've read a post about making BSD myth like cthulhu. It's one of the most refreshing idea. Books are the best inspirations in my opinion.<br /> For every tribe I can get something from the books. <br /> Examples:<br /> Black furies - Henry Lion Oldi - A Hero Must Be Alone<br /> Get of Fenrir - Marc Barrowcliffe - Wolfesangel series or two books about Siggrida Sotrrada by E. Cherezi\u0144ska (kicking ass) - not available in english version<br /> Glass walkers - the Godfather of course or any cyberpunk novel<br /> Fianna - Bernard Cornwell Saxon saga and Arthur saga<br /> Stargazers - Lian hearn - Ottori saga and similar stuff , very cool, but if you want to find something deeper and WtA style - only Rage across the Heavens i think<br /> Silver Fangs - Reborn kingdom E. Cherezi\u0144ska - not available in english version<br /> Shadow lords and Red talons - Markus Heitz - Ritus, Sanctum<br /> Bone gnawers - Mercy Thompson stuff - very light, fast to read, adventure - Patricia Briggs , I don't remember book about homeless altruists, maby some classic - La peste - Albert Camus<br /> Children of Gaia - seriously? Bible. Old testament.<br /> Uktena and Wendigo - historical books, there's many of them<br /> Silent Striders - truly everything with big adventure theme and! Cthulhu stuff<br /> <br /> It's only top of iceberg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:47:31-08:00","id":1044614,"title":"","content":"(This is true, and may serv to inpsir a WW game)<br /> <br /> This blurb of personal experience takes place In a city on the Texas Mexican border. This bordertown is the biggest inland port to the United States from Mexico.<br /> <br /> When I was a kid late 80's early 90's you could go to a well known flower and gifts shop in the hood that had a backroom full of cages ( not nice pet store cages).<br /> <br /> I remember to the locals it was no big deal what was happening in the back of the flower shop. They were either ignorant , undereducated, or were happy to be making money with what was happening in the back of the shop.<br /> <br /> I remember going into the back of the shop and seeing steel cages stacked on cages , animal filth everywhere and mice and rats darting under the cages and crawling all over everything.<br /> <br /> Inside the cages were TONS of exotic animals , A bald eagle , a spider monkey, a full grown caiman etc.. These animals were for sale....<br /> <br /> I remember in this same city for several years you would go out and about on the town , and wherever missing cat and missing dog flyers were , you would also see one too many flyers for missing monkeys with rewards for their return.<br /> <br /> This city also had way too many instances of Mexican immigrants going missing (no body) in the Rio Grande , right under the international bridge.<br /> <br /> When I got to college I found out why- The illegal animal trade is HUGE , but people usually just think of drugs and people trafficking. But what happens when a criminal transporting illegal animals approaches customs and feels the heating getting to strong? They release their cargo into the green space and the Rio Grande.<br /> <br /> It became such a problem that the local college set up a &quot;zoo&quot; of sorts along the border where the college students could go visit. It had ALL sortsa animals pulled from the Rio Grande that didn't belong there. Gators, Piranhas, Eagles, jungle cats, crocodiles , monkeys , lemurs, sting rays , exotic birds from the jungle etc...<br /> <br /> Many poor people trying to quickly cross that river were gobbled up because of the illegal pet trade.<br /> <br /> What drives this trade...well...its on the border of mexico , and drug dealers are very showy. It was not uncommon to have a residential area where someone owned a tiger cub or two in their backyard, a tank with a juvenile shark in it, hell my tattoo artist had a baby komodo dragon , This usually took place in that one house in the hood that happened to be a mansion surrounded by decrepid shacks.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T10:58:08-08:00","id":1045223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1041803-real-life-werewolf-the-apocalypse-inspiration?p=1042850#post1042850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get of Fenrir - Marc Barrowcliffe - Wolfesangel series or two books about Siggrida Sotrrada by E. Cherezi\u0144ska (kicking ass) - not available in english version<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs - Reborn kingdom E. Cherezi\u0144ska - not available in english version</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, now I wish I could read Polish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" tar